"""
Qwen3-ASR (Transformers-native ``*-hf``).

Default timing: TEN/FireRed VAD islands gate ASR windows (WhisperJAV-style
recall). Cue bounds prefer:
1. ForcedAligner acoustic stamps when requested (clamped to the island —
   not rescaled onto the full VAD span),
2. else PCM speech-active subspans inside the island (skip pad/silence),
3. else char-proportional paint on the VAD span.

After island ASR (default), ``ten_pcm`` re-times cues on the TEN timeline +
PCM subspans and runs waveform/onset/hold/clamp polish (Transub Pro). Disable
with ``vad.asrTiming=off`` or env ``TRANSUB_ENGINE_ASR_TIMING=off``.

ForcedAligner is opt-in via ``timingAlignModel`` containing ``align`` /
``qwen3-forced-aligner``. Fallback when TEN is unavailable: fixed windows +
sentence/CPS cue distribution (no aligner VRAM).

HF load / generate / align live in ``qwen3_hf_*.py``. Orchestration is split
across ``qwen3_{runtime,batch,policy,windows,cues,singing,errors,retry,infer,
island,windowed}.py`` — this module is the public facade + ``qwen3_asr_transcribe``.
"""

